What:           /sys/fs/btrfs/features/acl
Date:           July 2023
KernelVersion:  6.6
Contact:        linux-btrfs@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Indicates whether the running kernel's btrfs supports POSIX ACL.
		ACL support is controlled by the compile-time option
		CONFIG_BTRFS_FS_POSIX_ACL.

		Reading this file returns:
		   0 - ACL support not available
		   1 - ACL support available

		If the file does not exist, the kernel is too old to expose
		this interface. In that case, ACL support can only be
		determined by mounting and checking mount options.
Users:		btrfs-progs, fstests, system administration scripts

What:           /sys/fs/btrfs/features/block_group_tree
		/sys/fs/btrfs/<FSID>/features/block_group_tree
Date:           August 2022
KernelVersion:  6.1
Contact:        linux-btrfs@vger.kernel.org
Description:
                Read-only compatible feature flag indicating that the
                filesystem stores block group items in a dedicated
                BLOCK_GROUP_TREE (BGT), instead of in the EXTENT_TREE.

                This improves mount performance by avoiding a full block
                group item search during mount.

                Enabling this feature requires that the filesystem also has
                the free space cache v2 and no-holes features enabled. This
                restriction is intended to reduce testing combinations and
                encourage use of current default features.

		File exists:
		   Support is available in the kernel
		Reading this file returns:
		   0 - Undefined
		   1 - Filesystem is using the BGT
Users:          System administration scripts.

